.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt LIFE_CYCLE-CIPHER 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm life_cycle-cipher
.Nd The cipher algorithm life-cycle
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All symmetric ciphers (CIPHERs) go through a number of stages in their
life-cycle:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It start
This state represents the CIPHER before it has been allocated.
It is the starting state for any life-cycle transitions.
.It newed
This state represents the CIPHER after it has been allocated.
.It initialised
These states represent the CIPHER when it is set up and capable of
processing input.
There are three possible initialised states:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It initialised using EVP_CipherInit
.It initialised for decryption using EVP_DecryptInit
.It initialised for encryption using EVP_EncryptInit
.El
.It updated
These states represent the CIPHER when it is set up and capable of
processing additional input or generating output.
The three possible states directly correspond to those for initialised
above.
The three different streams should not be mixed.
.It finaled
This state represents the CIPHER when it has generated output.
.It freed
This state is entered when the CIPHER is freed.
It is the terminal state for all life-cycle transitions.
.El
